WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.937 --> 00:00:04.596
- Lion dancing dates back to
the Tang dynasty in China.

00:00:04.596 --> 00:00:06.615
It was really meant to
ward off the evil spirits

00:00:06.615 --> 00:00:08.466
and welcome the good ones.

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:11.269
I am a 20-something-year-old millennial,

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:14.555
but I still hold this piece of tradition.

00:00:14.555 --> 00:00:18.222
(drumming and shaker music)

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.522
Grab three rings and make three lines.

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:24.408
I was born and raised in Chinatown.

00:00:24.408 --> 00:00:27.180
We do have a lot of the Chinese traditions

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.424
that they've come over and carried on

00:00:28.424 --> 00:00:30.710
and passed on to us.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.642
Lion dancing is really
important to Chinatown

00:00:32.642 --> 00:00:34.858
because it is a traditional sport.

00:00:34.858 --> 00:00:37.268
It's something that a
lot of people do come out

00:00:37.268 --> 00:00:39.757
and they celebrate
around Chinese New Year.

00:00:39.757 --> 00:00:43.197
Typically includes at
least two people per set.

00:00:43.197 --> 00:00:45.805
In a lion, you'll have somebody
who plays the lion head

00:00:45.805 --> 00:00:48.700
and then somebody who'll play the tail.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.508
When you first some in,
you walk through the door,

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:52.528
you can't just pick up a lion head.

00:00:52.528 --> 00:00:55.716
It takes about a year
for you to be able to

00:00:55.716 --> 00:00:58.159
work your way up to that level.

00:00:58.159 --> 00:01:00.469
Kung Fu is the foundation of lion dance.

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:03.667
Their stances and their leg
work is extremely important.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.249
We're having you train in your footwork

00:01:05.249 --> 00:01:08.067
and your stances, making sure
that you're strong enough

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.486
to physically hold
yourself through a routine

00:01:10.486 --> 00:01:13.534
but also a lion head,
'cause a lion head is heavy.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:17.534
It's typically anywhere
between 15 to 30 pounds.

00:01:18.976 --> 00:01:21.964
(man drums rapidly)

00:01:21.964 --> 00:01:24.836
Typically we teach different routines

00:01:24.836 --> 00:01:27.013
for each of the lions just because

00:01:27.013 --> 00:01:29.132
you never know which
one you're gonna play.

00:01:29.132 --> 00:01:31.882
(drumming music)

00:01:33.518 --> 00:01:35.066
You can see us lion
dancing in the streets.

00:01:35.066 --> 00:01:37.700
Anytime where there's a community event

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.733
we'll usually partake in them.

00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:42.364
In Chinatown a lot of people
are familiar with lion dancing

00:01:42.364 --> 00:01:44.590
and they get really
pumped and excited for it.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.778
So just the energy and
the atmosphere for me

00:01:46.778 --> 00:01:48.445
is ten times better.

00:01:49.621 --> 00:01:51.726
It's really important for all of us that

00:01:51.726 --> 00:01:54.446
we are educated about lion dancing,

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:57.112
we do carry it on just because it is

00:01:57.112 --> 00:02:00.059
kind of a lost art here in America.

00:02:00.059 --> 00:02:01.826
For me, when I do have children one day,

00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:04.691
I would like to pass
that on to them as well.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:05.624
I think it's really important.

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:08.605
I think it's what makes
our family our family.

00:02:08.605 --> 00:02:11.188
(string music)

00:02:14.703 --> 00:02:17.536
(electronic beep)

